  "caption": "Deadline day: Quinn sat head-forward, shoulders up, for five hours straight — and by 4pm the neck felt like a rusty gate. A quick search about text neck did not help.\n\nDesk-job neck pain is mostly about long, still positions and tired deep neck muscles rather than damage. Stress and poor sleep can turn the volume up.\n\nWhat can help: movement breaks every 30–45 minutes, chin nods and band rows, a screen at eye level with forearms supported, and building strength rather than only stretching.\n\nGet it checked if pain spreads below the elbow, you get pins and needles in the hand, new or changing headaches appear, or there's no improvement after 2–3 weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
